","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"இருவர்","parts":[{"text":"இருவர்","lemma":"iruvar","gloss":"two persons"}],"gloss":"two lovers"},{"surface":"அல்லது","parts":[{"text":"அல்லது","lemma":"allatu","gloss":"except"}],"gloss":"except"},{"surface":"யாமத்துத்","parts":[{"text":"யாமத்துத்","lemma":"யாமத்துத்","gloss":"at midnight"}],"gloss":"at midnight","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தனிமகன்","parts":[{"text":"தனி","lemma":"taṉi","gloss":"lone"},{"text":"மகன்","lemma":"makaṉ","gloss":"man"}],"gloss":"lone man"},{"surface":"வழங்காப்","parts":[{"text":"வழங்கா","lemma":"vaḻaṅkā","gloss":"not walking"},{"text":"ப்","lemma":"p","gloss":"consonant"}],"gloss":"not walking"},{"surface":"பனிமலர்க்","parts":[{"text":"பனி","lemma":"paṉi","gloss":"cool/dewy"},{"text":"மலர்","lemma":"malar","gloss":"flower"},{"text":"க்","lemma":"k","gloss":"consonant"}],"gloss":"cool flower"},{"surface":"காவின்","parts":[{"text":"கா","lemma":"kā","gloss":"grove"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"in"}],"gloss":"in the grove"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஒதுக்குஇன்","parts":[{"text":"ஒதுக்கு","lemma":"otukku","gloss":"secluded"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"of"}],"gloss":"secluded"},{"surface":"திணிமணல்","parts":[{"text":"திணி","lemma":"tiṇi","gloss":"dense"},{"text":"மணல்","lemma":"maṇal","gloss":"sand"}],"gloss":"dense sand"},{"surface":"புதுப்பூம்","parts":[{"text":"புது","lemma":"putu","gloss":"fresh"},{"text":"பூ","lemma":"pū","gloss":"flower"},{"text":"ம்","lemma":"m","gloss":"consonant"}],"gloss":"fresh flower"},{"surface":"பள்ளி","parts":[{"text":"பள்ளி","lemma":"paḷḷi","gloss":"bed/resting place"}],"gloss":"bed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வாயின்","parts":[{"text":"வாய்","lemma":"vāy","gloss":"gate/entrance"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"at"}],"gloss":"at the gates"},{"surface":"மாடந்தொறும்","parts":[{"text":"மாடம்","lemma":"māṭam","gloss":"mansion/tower"},{"text":"தொறும்","lemma":"toṟum","gloss":"every"}],"gloss":"in every mansion"},{"surface":"மைவிடை","parts":[{"text":"மை","lemma":"mai","gloss":"black"},{"text":"விடை","lemma":"viṭai","gloss":"ram"}],"gloss":"black ram"},{"surface":"வீழ்ப்ப","parts":[{"text":"வீழ்ப்ப","lemma":"vīḻppa","gloss":"to slay/sacrifice"}],"gloss":"to sacrifice"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நீஆங்குக்","parts":[{"text":"நீஆங்குக்","lemma":"நீஆங்குக்","gloss":"you there"}],"gloss":"you there","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கொண்ட","parts":[{"text":"கொண்ட","lemma":"koṇṭa","gloss":"celebrated"}],"gloss":"celebrated"},{"surface":"விழவினும்","parts":[{"text":"விழவு","lemma":"viḻavu","gloss":"festival"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"than"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"even"}],"gloss":"than the festivals"},{"surface":"பலவே","parts":[{"text":"பல","lemma":"pala","gloss":"many"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"are many indeed"}]}],"literal":"Forest-dwelling life furious-dog hunter / deer-meat poured basket-and cowherd-woman / curd-with came pot-and to-fill / plough-by those-who-live large-house women / pond-below grown field-gathered white-paddy / scooped-they to-give rejoiced-they returning / southern lord-of-hills poor-land-within-even / seven-fortress door battering capturing your / gaping-mouth tiger engraving strength / singers Vaṉci to-sing soldiers / dusty-manure street army-camp to-shine / unfading green-leaves inserting-in-between strung / unblossomed garland ball resembling / meat-rice abundance large-family feeding / noble-nature-is-it ah! your fierce-battlefront camp / expert-artisan fashioned beautiful-lines having / lily doll dancing-beauty resembling / love two-persons except midnight / lone-man not-walking cool-flower grove-in / secluded dense-sand fresh-flower bed / gate mansion-every black-ram to-sacrifice / you-there celebrated festivals-than many-indeed","translation":"The hunter of the forest, accompanied by his furious dogs, pours deer meat into the basket of the cowherd woman, and she fills his pot with the curd she brought. The women of the spacious houses of the farmers who live by the plough scoop up and give white paddy grown below the pond and gathered from the fields, and they return rejoicing. Even in the poor land of the southern lord of the hills, you battered the doors of the seven fortresses, captured them, and engraved your gaping-mouthed tiger emblem. Your strength is such that while singers sing Vaṉci songs and soldiers shine in the army camp on the dusty streets, you feed your large family of kinsmen with abundant meat-rice that resembles a ball of unblossomed garland strung with unfading green leaves inserted in between. Ah, your fierce battlefront camp is of noble nature! In the cool flower groves where no lone man walks at midnight except for two lovers, on the secluded dense sand beds of fresh flowers, black rams are sacrificed at every mansion gate. The sacrifices offered there are indeed more numerous than the festivals you celebrated!","modern":"காட்டில் வாழும் வேட்டைக்காரன் தன் சினமுள்ள நாய்களுடன் வந்து வேட்டையாடிய மான் இறைச்சியை இடைமகளின் கூடையில் கொட்டுகிறான். அதற்குப் பதிலாக அவள் தன் தயிர்ப் பானையிலிருந்து தயிரை அவனுக்குத் தருகிறாள். உழவர்களின் பெரிய வீட்டுப் பெண்கள் குளத்து நீரில் விளைந்த வெண்ணெல்லை அள்ளித் தர, அதைப் பெற்றுக்கொண்டு அவர்கள் மகிழ்ந்து செல்கிறார்கள். தென்னாட்டிற்குரிய பாண்டியனின் வளம் குறைந்த நாட்டிலும், நீ ஏழு கோட்டைகளின் கதவுகளைத் தகர்த்து, அவற்றைக் கைப்பற்றி, உனது பெரிய வாயையுடைய புலிச் சின்னத்தைப் பொறித்தாய். உனது ஆற்றலைப் பாணர்கள் வஞ்சிப் பாடல்களாகப் பாட, வீரர்கள் புழுதி நிறைந்த தெருக்களையுடைய பாசறையில் விளங்குகிறார்கள். வாடாத பச்சிலைகளைக் கொண்டு கட்டிய அரும்புகள் நிறைந்த மாலைப் பந்தைப் போன்ற இறைச்சிச் சோற்றைத் தன் சுற்றத்தாருக்கு வழங்கி மகிழ்விக்கிறான் சோழன் நலங்கிள்ளி. உனது போர்முனைப் பாசறை மிகவும் பெருமைக்குரியது! நள்ளிரவில் காதலர்கள் இருவரைத் தவிர வேறு யாரும் நடமாடாத குளிர்ந்த சோலையில், மணல் பரப்பிய மலர்ப் படுக்கைகளில், மாளிகைகளின் வாயில்தோறும் கரிய ஆட்டுக்கிடாக்கள் பலியிடப்படுகின்றன. நீ அங்கே கொண்டாடிய விழாக்களைக் காட்டிலும் இப்பலிகள் பலவாகும்.","explanation":"This poem is addressed to the Chola king Nalaṅkiḷḷi by the poet Kōvūr Kiḻār, belonging to the Vaakai tiṇai (victory/excellence) and the theme of Arasavaakai (the king's victory and noble deeds). The poet praises the king's military prowess and his generosity. The poem begins by describing the peaceful exchange of goods in the countryside: a forest hunter exchanges deer meat for curd from a cowherd woman, and farmers' wives generously distribute white paddy. This peaceful prosperity is contrasted with the king's fierce military campaigns in the south, where he captured seven fortresses and engraved his tiger emblem. In the army camp, the king feeds his soldiers and kinsmen with abundant meat-rice, described beautifully as resembling a ball of unblossomed flower garland. Finally, the poet describes the sacrifices of black rams at the gates of every mansion in the captured territory, noting that these sacrifices are even more numerous than the festivals celebrated by the king, highlighting his absolute dominance and the scale of his victory.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}